      "writtenOn": "2024-07-12T20:03:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In case input was unsorted and then lets assume split happened in first so before will be [1Group_firstPart] and after will be [1Group_secondPart] and now lets say second group is completely before then [1Group_firstPart, secondGroup] and after will be [1Group_secondPart]\n\nNow as we know these groups are rendered in order in UI making [1Group_firstPart, secondGroup, 1Group_secondPart] as a result which will not be correct. As wherever a split happens it has to be rendered in order. \n\nSo my assumption is this method is always called for sorted groups and that\u0027s what I have seen in gr-diff-processor.",
