      "writtenOn": "2024-07-12T20:03:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. I agree mostly this is called for only 1 group which is also unchanged as any changed group before or after will not be considered for collapse. Only cases where multiple groups will come is when there is a common group (ignoreWhiteSpace) or there is a skip group.\n\n2. Going with the assumption that wherever a split happens the end result should be \n[..something1, ...something2, splittedGroup_firstPart] and after should be [splittedGroup_secondPart, something3, something3] so this makes sure once a split is done, nothing should be added to beforeGroup and it can only go in afterGroup.\n\n3. Now going with above point, in case split is not done till now, the only place a delta should go is beforeGroup or else if we put this in afterGroup then when a split is done afterGroup will look like [delta_which_is_not_split, splitGroup_seconfPart] thus agin breaking the assumption of from a split first part should be last element of beforeGroup and secondPart of split should be first group of afterGroups.\n\n\n\nNow what you have suggested (code) was my earlier solution but this breaks down for cases like [Only additions] thus it will not have start_line or end_line on left side making delta group to be pushed to beforeGroup even though split was done it should go in afterGroup.\n\nRule that I am following is: Wherever a split happens, its first part should be last entry of beforeGroup and second part should be first entry of afterGroup.",
      "parentUuid": "db19e666_b5b44a85",
